#. type: Title =
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "OpenEMS: Weather"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
msgid ""
"OpenEMS gets weather data from the **Open-Meteo** service. The data is "
"mainly needed for the xref:user/schedule/forecasts.adoc[solar yield "
"forecast]. The web interface also uses it to show the current weather and a "
"forecast."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-setup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
msgid ""
"The function is called **Weather.OpenMeteo** and has **no settings of its "
"own**."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-setup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
msgid ""
"The **location** comes from the system settings (Meta). It must be correct "
"there, otherwise the solar forecast will not match."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-setup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
msgid ""
"An **access key** is not required. Without a key, the freely usable Open-"
"Meteo access is used. The commercial access is only used if a manufacturer "
"supplies its own key."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-setup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
msgid "The system needs internet access."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Which data"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-which-data
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
msgid ""
"**Forecast for 7 days**, in quarter hours: solar irradiation (total, direct, "
"diffuse), temperature, snowfall and snow depth."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-which-data
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
msgid ""
"Hourly and daily: weather condition (symbol), temperature, minimum and "
"maximum values, sunshine duration."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-which-data
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
msgid ""
"**Past weather:** To train the solar forecast, weather data of past days at "
"the location is also retrieved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "How often it is updated"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-often-it-is-updated
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
msgid "Immediately at startup."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-often-it-is-updated
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
msgid ""
"After that **every 3 hours**, with a random delay of up to 5 minutes. The "
"random delay prevents all systems from sending requests at the same time."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-often-it-is-updated
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
msgid "If a request fails, it is retried after about 10 to 70 seconds."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-how-often-it-is-updated
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
msgid ""
"If the forecast is outdated, it is no longer used. The basis for the solar "
"forecast is then also missing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What you see in OpenEMS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Value\n"
"| Meaning\n"
"\n"
"| Current temperature\n"
"| in °C\n"
"| Current weather condition\n"
"| as a weather code (symbol)\n"
"| Sunshine duration today\n"
"| in seconds\n"
"| Minimum/maximum temperature today\n"
"| in °C\n"
"| HTTP status\n"
"| Result of the last request (helps with troubleshooting)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
msgid ""
"In addition, forecast values are stored every hour, so they can be seen "
"later in the history."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "If something is wrong"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-if-something-is-wrong
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
msgid ""
"**Solar forecast does not match at all:** First check the location in the "
"system settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-if-something-is-wrong
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
msgid "**No weather data:** Check the internet connection and the HTTP status."
msgstr ""
